## 10. MOST ASKED INTERVIEW QUESTIONS

**Q. What problem does Proxy solve?**

Controls access to the real object.

---

**Q. Does Proxy change business logic?**

No. It only controls access.

---

**Q. Which SOLID principle does it follow?**

Open/Closed Principle (OCP).

---

**Q. Does Proxy use composition?**

Yes. Proxy **HAS-A** Real Subject.

---

## 11. PROXY vs DECORATOR

| Proxy             | Decorator             |
| ----------------- | --------------------- |
| Controls access   | Adds new behavior     |
| Security, caching | Extends functionality |

---

## 12. INTERVIEW ONE-LINER

**Proxy provides a surrogate object that controls access to the real object by adding security, 
lazy loading, caching, or logging without modifying the real object.**

#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

//=====================
// SUBJECT
//=====================

class Folder
{
public:
    virtual void readWrite() = 0;
    virtual ~Folder() = default;
};

//=====================
// REAL SUBJECT
//=====================

class RealFolder : public Folder
{
public:
    void readWrite() override
    {
        cout << "Read/Write operation allowed." << endl;
    }
};

//=====================
// USER
//=====================

class User
{
private:
    string role;

public:
    User(string r) : role(r)
    {
    }

    string getRole() const
    {
        return role;
    }
};

//=====================
// PROXY
//=====================

class ProxyFolder : public Folder
{
private:
    Folder* folder;
    User* user;

public:
    ProxyFolder(User* u)
        : folder(nullptr), user(u)
    {
    }

    ~ProxyFolder()
    {
        delete folder;
    }

    void readWrite() override
    {
        if (user->getRole() == "Manager")
        {
            folder = new RealFolder();
            folder->readWrite();
        }
        else
        {
            cout << "Access Denied!" << endl;
        }
    }
};

//=====================
// CLIENT
//=====================

int main()
{
    User* developer = new User("Developer");
    User* manager = new User("Manager");

    Folder* f1 = new ProxyFolder(developer);
    Folder* f2 = new ProxyFolder(manager);

    f1->readWrite();
    f2->readWrite();

    delete f1;
    delete f2;
    delete developer;
    delete manager;

    return 0;
}
